<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo Heavy final '96 net plunges.</title>
<headline>Daewoo Heavy final '96 net plunges.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>							    1996	 1995</p>
<p>    Net profit					 74.78 vs   129.48</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	common shares				   5.0  vs     5.0</p>
<p>	preferred shares				6.0  vs     6.0</p>
<p>    Shr (won)					 201    vs   354</p>
<p>    Turnover					5,148.51 vs 3,963.04</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				  114.51 vs   168.34</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (both loss)		   7.06 vs    32.22</p>
<p>NOTE - Daewoo Heavy Industries Ltd, an affiliate of the Daewoo Group, manufactures ships, industrial plants and machinery. The company's share capital increased by 36,982 shares to 367.59 million in calendar 1996 due to conversion of convertible bonds. The final figures were in line with the company's estimates released early this month.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
